  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From and until",
     "texto": [
      "**das nove às cinco** (from nine to five): **das** means «from the» and **às** means «at the».",
      "**Até** (until) indicates the end: **até às seis** (until six).",
      "**A partir de** (from) indicates the start: **a partir das dez** (from ten o'clock)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Duration and approximation",
     "texto": [
      "**Durante** (for, during) indicates how long something lasts: **durante uma hora** (for an hour).",
      "**Por volta de** (around): **por volta das oito** (around eight)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking about a timetable",
     "texto": [
      "You can ask **A que horas abre a loja?** (what time does the shop open?) or **A que horas é que a loja abre?**",
      "**Que horas?**, **quanto tempo?** and **até que horas?** ask about the time or the duration. The construction with **é que** is common in European Portuguese; you don't need to use it in every question."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
